      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 2 - Rewrite a prompt with the 27B LoRA\n\nThe node this pack is named after. It runs LightX2V's MiniMax-H3 prompt\nrewriter LoRA on Qwen3.6-27B -- an adapter trained on this exact job,\nwhich is why its prose reads like the prompts MiniMax ships.\n\n## What it needs\n\nA 27B model, fetched on the first run. The list starts at 10 GB and\nends at 52 GB; this template picks **GGUF Q4_K_M**, a 15.7 GB download\nthat wants about 19 GB of VRAM with the adapter attached. Nothing has\nto be installed for it -- without `llama-cpp-python` the node fetches\nthe official llama.cpp binaries by itself.\n\n**If it does not fit:** lower **gpu_layers** on the options node (-1 is\nall of them) and the rest runs on the CPU, slower. Or open\n*1 - Write a prompt*, which does the same job with a 2.6 GB model.\n\n## The options node\n\nUnplug it and nothing changes: every value on it is the default the\nnodes use anyway. It is there for the four things worth reaching for --\n**gpu_layers** to fit a smaller card, **device** to send the writer to\na second GPU, **self_check** to decide how much the nodes say out loud,\nand **fix_once** to let them repair what the check found instead of\nonly reporting it.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Put a short idea into **prompt**. One sentence is enough.\n2. Set **duration** to the length of the clip you are going to make --\n   in both nodes.\n3. Run. The rewrite comes out on the right.\n\nThe outputs match *1 - Write a prompt* one for one, so the two nodes\nare interchangeable anywhere in a graph."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
